mments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/659348318400aa7ea090a71ee6dcc729eb370be8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-06T16:05:36Z","email":"35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"aknagar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-06T16:05:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/test auth production parity (#70)\n\n* fix: configure Azure Entra ID auth for production via Microsoft.Identity.Web\n\nReplace the placeholder throw in Program.cs with AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApiAuthentication().\n- Add Microsoft.Identity.Web 3.8.2 package (and bump IdentityModel deps to 8.7.0)\n- Auth is now environment-branched: Dev/Test keeps the lenient JWT scheme;\n  Production validates Bearer tokens against Azure Entra ID using the AzureAd\n  config section (Instance, TenantId, ClientId, Audience)\n- Add AzureAd skeleton section to appsettings.json with placeholder values\n\n* docs: add Entra ID API protection guide\n\nCovers every step to register the API and a client app in Azure Entra ID,\nwhere to find TenantId/ClientId/Audience, how to protect endpoints with\n[Authorize]/scopes/roles, environment-specific config, token inspection,\nand a troubleshooting section.\n\n* fix: wire up production-parity JWT auth in Test environment\n\n- Remove Test env bypass from Program.cs; Test now uses\n  AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApiAuthentication (same as Production).\n- Skip DefaultAzureCredential, KeyVault, and ServiceBus Aspire\n  registrations in the Test environment to prevent IMDS probe hangs.\n- Add TestAuthConstants + ReplaceWithTestJwtHandler (Common/Auth)\n  which swaps Entra ID''s JwtBearer validator for a local HS256 one.\n- Add TestTokenFactory with CreateToken/CreateAdminToken/\n  CreateExpiredToken helpers for generating test Bearer tokens.\n- Rewrite WeatherEndpointTests and RateLimitingIntegrationTests to\n  use authenticated clients; add 401-without-token and\n  401-with-expired-token coverage.\n- Uncomment .RequireAuthorization() on GET /weather/{date} so\n  unauthenticated requests correctly return 401.\n- Fix CreateExpiredToken to set both notBefore and expires in the\n  past so JwtSecurityToken does not throw IDX12401.\n\n* fix: remove IsDevelopment auth bypass, use Entra ID for all environments\n\nThe lenient dev-only JWT block (no signature validation, auto-created\ntest user) is removed. AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApiAuthentication now\nruns unconditionally for every environment including Development.\n\nAlso removes the unused JwtBearer, IdentityModel.Tokens, and System.Text\nusing directives that were only needed by the dev bypass.","tree":{"sha":"e28e2511cb983e0e87c5d79670549a5e0faaeb4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/trees/e28e2511cb983e0e87c5d79670549a5e0faaeb4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/commits/659348318400aa7ea090a71ee6dcc729eb370be8","verification":{"payload":"tree e28e2511cb983e0e87c5d79670549a5e0faaeb4d\nparent f7873c108e8a606436c567dfd802bd4fc1151044\nauthor aknagar <35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com> 1775491536 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775491536 +0530\n\nFix/test auth production parity (#70)\n\n* fix: configure Azure Entra ID auth for production via Microsoft.Identity.Web\n\nReplace the placeholder throw in Program.cs with AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApiAuthentication().\n- Add Microsoft.Identity.Web 3.8.2 package (and bump IdentityModel deps to 8.7.0)\n- Auth is now environment-branched: Dev/Test keeps the lenient JWT scheme;\n  Production validates Bearer tokens against Azure Entra ID using the AzureAd\n  config section (Instance, TenantId, ClientId, Audience)\n- Add AzureAd skeleton section to appsettings.json with placeholder values\n\n* docs: add Entra ID API protection guide\n\nCovers every step to register the API and a client app in Azure Entra ID,\nwhere to find TenantId/ClientId/Audience, how to protect endpoints with\n[Authorize]/scopes/roles, environment-specific config, token inspection,\nand a troubleshooting section.\n\n* fix: wire up production-parity JWT auth in Test environment\n\n- Remove Test env bypass from Program.cs; Test now uses\n  AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApiAuthentication (same as Production).\n- Skip DefaultAzureCredential, KeyVault, and ServiceBus Aspire\n  registrations in the Test environment to prevent IMDS probe hangs.\n- Add TestAuthConstants + ReplaceWithTestJwtHandler (Common/Auth)\n  which swaps Entra ID''s JwtBearer validator for a local HS256 one.\n- Add TestTokenFactory with CreateToken/CreateAdminToken/\n  CreateExpiredToken helpers for generating test Bearer tokens.\n- Rewrite WeatherEndpointTests and RateLimitingIntegrationTests to\n  use authenticated clients; add 401-without-token and\n  401-with-expired-token coverage.\n- Uncomment .RequireAuthorization() on GET /weather/{date} so\n  unauthenticated requests correctly return 401.\n- Fix CreateExpiredToken to set both notBefore and expires in the\n  past so JwtSecurityToken does not throw IDX12401.\n\n* fix: remove IsDevelopment auth bypass, use Entra ID for all environments\n\nThe lenient dev-only JWT block (no signature validation, auto-created\ntest user) is removed. AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApiAuthentication now\nruns unconditionally for every environment including Development.\n\nAlso removes the unused JwtBearer, IdentityModel.Tokens, and System.Text\nusing directives that were only needed by the dev bypass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp09nQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWLIQABnIPAtrj3uH7QCpEcZ5O4iW\nTtCd8l4HGCBRccaXHOhDHJxo5rVva+9gPvnu762jrpOseN9RL64PQ5VNBN/WqlHJ\nNQjzW7osfNi5PBXtLLZIN0GTTLIzL6TB78aaZb3K4DTisauK9SYTtE+gJ/5u5CoA\n7heILpsbcXWE+JyCRGhuyUmJV5QHeH4iFGWAlIlPzrOdnbCAcrdZXngUZbSIeca8\nVmxxQKIodAgiHkosO9CDXqh5pmTtV7z6Xgo2+jqrslSu/BSVOX5BygWG4HXa3L1r\n5yqyizIJaODSIl9vvsmZ39x7fPSUX2LcLlbYBM7EeVF5tybpIXO9K0z2MijIJkrC\nPV+EDtjHXZyGbIuLgRKVN1rMeq5RXJg6Lo3Uw2e+n0xnjiJ6/AzOBH/NHDV4u3L7\nLfl