6VXNlcjM1Njc5OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/a19a81c7fc53e796ca0f5a104e87d1ebfe449d89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-06T15:14:13Z","email":"35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"aknagar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-06T15:14:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/azure ad auth (#69)\n\n* fix: configure Azure Entra ID auth for production via Microsoft.Identity.Web\n\nReplace the placeholder throw in Program.cs with AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApiAuthentication().\n- Add Microsoft.Identity.Web 3.8.2 package (and bump IdentityModel deps to 8.7.0)\n- Auth is now environment-branched: Dev/Test keeps the lenient JWT scheme;\n  Production validates Bearer tokens against Azure Entra ID using the AzureAd\n  config section (Instance, TenantId, ClientId, Audience)\n- Add AzureAd skeleton section to appsettings.json with placeholder values\n\n* docs: add Entra ID API protection guide\n\nCovers every step to register the API and a client app in Azure Entra ID,\nwhere to find TenantId/ClientId/Audience, how to protect endpoints with\n[Authorize]/scopes/roles, environment-specific config, token inspection,\nand a troubleshooting section.","tree":{"sha":"71ee601473945bd2131f1776bf946d060289e19b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/trees/71ee601473945bd2131f1776bf946d060289e19b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/commits/a19a81c7fc53e796ca0f5a104e87d1ebfe449d89","verification":{"payload":"tree 71ee601473945bd2131f1776bf946d060289e19b\nparent a047a5c27be28005c98fe33df9b3da65eda80574\nauthor aknagar <35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com> 1775488453 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775488453 +0530\n\nFix/azure ad auth (#69)\n\n* fix: configure Azure Entra ID auth for production via Microsoft.Identity.Web\n\nReplace the placeholder throw in Program.cs with AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApiAuthentication().\n- Add Microsoft.Identity.Web 3.8.2 package (and bump IdentityModel deps to 8.7.0)\n- Auth is now environment-branched: Dev/Test keeps the lenient JWT scheme;\n  Production validates Bearer tokens against Azure Entra ID using the AzureAd\n  config section (Instance, TenantId, ClientId, Audience)\n- Add AzureAd skeleton section to appsettings.json with placeholder values\n\n* docs: add Entra ID API protection guide\n\nCovers every step to register the API and a client app in Azure Entra ID,\nwhere to find TenantId/ClientId/Audience, how to protect endpoints with\n[Authorize]/scopes/roles, environment-specific config, token inspection,\nand a troubleshooting section.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp083FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjQ0QAEjf+qNUKK2P6DoUCCVbGkaB\nxz8EjHZgmvzJW8OYTz74pv3b0FVvf5Up/QtGogfvF9m3bRvYz2JGAC7ratJvp3y7\nYhoqd1Brnk4zxazF7WXd5Mw8gEg9E27Ea01+QjoOA2tY4EEMGRK1wqK/L2Mb3t0x\nHC9Y3R4s0YjBWmHE7ARH5+8lTbzjf0we27TEQZyYA+q2JPee1pf4sI/lNSLu8PBv\nOjs42ldCBxur0l4bIZRsEEya5WPeKUSWbzRF5ga3Qmgdzu9yO3LpSL3zMY6aj+7w\n/v7BqevVQy8qiVbaa+9gHn1ocpO+DpRhNtNQ/tu8OURS8lVhGPu4nUSEczG4a+by\nJ6beSKxcKBdLCMWq1Fryk6Wumj65om9QAPhjUns/YDRO7PqZAkAvGyQy4fqULYeG\nNeF60nSDtyUXUcIA1w8McjFVUl0C2n5GMVicXaRqwxHE93QQP5TardtIZr2F57cK\nnUPti1ywWjCzfiN3AAHZqayMUmVLr3K10T13GV2NVloai/CPTWV1Kf4l8ySKPKZ5\ntIkXzrIqZ83jB3VXbnMb08/jlRR/n0iiEE+bkQ5QjOwdVoooM3N+5JA4slORwZUx\nIaDJqCbCPHteTazZIlR5ChlqbK92lwDbC/+Y2NRuKFSwhjcTEprXTwcJ95knHYLQ\nICm6GK+9feYOJZeT0Mkh\n=WK8X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-06T15:14:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/a19a81c7fc53e796ca0f5a104e87d1ebfe449d89","node_id":"C_kwDOQv8lUNoAKGExOWE4MWM3ZmM1M2U3OTZjYTBmNWExMDRlODdkMWViZmU0NDlkODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/a047a5c27be28005c98fe33df9b3da65eda80574","sha":"a047a5c27be28005c98fe33df9b3da65eda80574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/a047a5c27be28005c98fe33df9b3da65eda80574"}],"sha":"a19a81c7fc53e796ca0f5a104e87d1ebfe449d89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/a19a81c7fc53e796ca0f5a104e87d1ebfe449d89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35679913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar","id":35679913,"login":"aknagar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc5OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/a047a5c27be28005c98fe33df9b3da65eda80574/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-31T02:57:36Z","email":"35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"aknagar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-31T02:57:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/aspire publish stuck (#68)\n\n* fix: remove --parameter flags from aspire deploy to unblock process-parameters step\n\nThe process-parameters pipeline step hangs indefinitely when --parameter flags\nreference names that don''t exist as builder.AddParameter() declarations in the\nAppHost. postgres uses Aspire-managed credentials (not user-supplied parameters)\nand daprRedis uses Azure Managed Redis with Entra ID (Password is null in Azure).\nRemoved postgres-password and redis-password --parameter flags from both the\ntest and prod deploy workflows. Also added timeout-minutes: 30 to the Deploy\napplication step as a safety net, and downgraded --log-level from trace to debug.\n\n* fix: set ASPIRE_INTERACTIVITY_ENABLED=false on deploy step to prevent CI hang\n\nThe process-parameters pipeline step hangs indefinitely in CI because the\nAppHost''s InteractionService.IsAvailable returns true when\nASPIRE_INTERACTIVITY_ENABLED is not explicitly disabled. With IsAvailable=true,\nParameterProcessor enters an interactive prompt loop for unresolved parameters\n(postgres-password) and waits on a CompletionTcs that is never signalled in a\nno-TTY CI environment.\n\nSetting ASPIRE_INTERACTIVITY_ENABLED=false on the Deploy application step''s\nenv block makes the variable visible to the AppHost subprocess (launched by\naspire deploy), so InteractionService.IsAvailable returns false and the\nprocessor uses the GenerateParameterDefault directly instead of prompting.\n\nDOTNET_ASPIRE_NONINTERACTIVE only controls CLI output/spinners and is not\nread by the AppHost''s InteractionService — it is not sufficient on its own.\n\n* docs: add root cause analysis for aspire deploy CI hang\n\n* fix: add aspire publish --non-interactive VS Code task\n\nPrevents aspire publish from hanging at process-parameters step.\nThe postgres-password secret parameter triggers an interactive prompt\nthat is hidden by the Aspire CLI TUI, causing the command to appear\nfrozen. --non-interactive auto-accepts generated defaults, skipping\nthe prompt.\n\n* fix: skip Dapr WithMetadata(IValueProvider) in publish mode to prevent process-parameters hang\n\nBicepOutputReference.GetValueAsync awaits ProvisioningTaskCompletionSource which is\nonly resolved after the ''provision-*'' pipeline steps — which run AFTER ''process-parameters''.\nCalling GetValueAsync inside the EnvironmentCallbackAnnotation that DaprDistributedApplicationLifecycleHook\nunconditionally adds to the DaprSidecarResource causes a silent deadlock.\n\nGuard the redisHost/redisPort/redisPassword WithMetadata calls with IsPublishMode check.\nThese metadata values are only needed for the live Dapr sidecar process (run mode), not\nfor manifest generation. The sidecar CLI itself is already excluded from publish mode.","tree":{"sha":"a02534c73bdba431e63a4dfbf5aaf7bdceb86f07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/trees/a02534c73bdba431e63a4dfbf5aaf7bdceb86f07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/commits/a047a5c27be28005c98fe33df9b3da65eda80574","verification":{"payload":"tree a02534c73bdba431e63a4dfbf5aaf7bdceb86f07\nparent 84e15782fa78dfd501a536244fec2183ac1f68e6\nauthor aknagar <35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com> 1774925856 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774925856 +0530\n\nFix/aspire publish stuck (#68)\n\n* fix: remove --parameter flags from aspire deploy to unblock process-parameters step\n\nThe process-parameters pipeline step hangs indefinitely when --parameter flags\nreference names that don''t exist as builder.AddParameter() declarations in the\nAppHost. postgres uses Aspire-managed credentials (not user-supplied parameters)\nand daprRedis uses Azure Managed Redis with Entra ID (Password is null in Azure).\nRemoved postgres-password and redis-password --parameter flags from both the\ntest and prod deploy workflows. Also added timeout-minutes: 30 to the Deploy\napplication step as a safety net, and downgraded --log-level from trace to debug.\n\n* fix: set ASPIRE_INTERACTIVITY_ENABLED=false on deploy step to prevent CI hang\n\nThe process-parameters pipeline step hangs indefinitely in CI because the\nAppHost''s InteractionService.IsAvailable returns true when\nASPIRE_INTERACTIVITY_ENABLED is not explicitly disabled. With IsAvailable=true,\nParameterProcessor enters an interactive prompt loop for unresolved parameters\n(postgres-password) and waits on a CompletionTcs that is never signalled in a\nno-TTY CI environment.\n\nSetting ASPIRE_INTERACTIVITY_ENABLED=false on the Deploy application step''s\nenv block makes the variable visible to the AppHost subprocess (launched by\naspire deploy), so InteractionService.IsAvailable returns false and the\nprocessor uses the GenerateParameterDefault directly instead of prompting.\n\nDOTNET_ASPIRE_NONINTERACTIVE only controls CLI output/spinners and is not\nread by the AppHost''s InteractionService — it is not sufficient on its own.\n\n* docs: add root cause analysis for aspire deploy CI hang\n\n* fix: add aspire publish --non-interactive VS Code task\n\nPrevents aspire publish from hanging at process-parameters step.\nThe postgres-password secret parameter triggers an interactive prompt\nthat is hidden by the Aspire CLI TUI, causing the command to appear\nfrozen. --non-interactive auto-accepts generated defaults, skipping\nthe prompt.\n\n* fix: skip Dapr WithMetadata(IValueProvider) in publish mode to prevent process-parameters hang\n\nBicepOutputReference.GetValueAsync awaits ProvisioningTaskCompletionSource which is\nonly resolved after the ''provision-*'' pipeline steps — which run AFTER ''process-parameters''.\nCalling GetValueAsync inside the EnvironmentCallbackAnnotation that DaprDistributedApplicationLifecycleHook\nunconditionally adds to the DaprSidecarResource causes a silent deadlock.\n\nGuard the redisHost/redisPort/redisPassword WithMetadata calls with IsPublishMode check.\nThese metadata values are only needed for the live Dapr sidecar process (run mode), not\nfor manifest generation. The sidecar CLI itself is already excluded from publish mode.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpyzggCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsV4QADVe+YX+XX94d32BbLMF5fla\nWOkLpLGwkoG5YxiMlDl9340tHd/zlgWm2O1aUI4Q0sbwTpQH8duKRxmLGuSlQnR6\nXJDYVbQii7SCC2stYwMHF3DW6bRkdbuo8QM8xNJpAR5QbEg+19u6CifOkICq4Uef\n5V9gwlPuARHDbaXIn5rTIFygv3ylpuf02Ytu3jwKbtXSeT+8C8hSgE5nB1TJ0NCh\nmC4JMnEpMiodTnyrZlLcm2qN4Qrw7EUjTaTFXiYq/rBeWCss8o0/db9figHdEDnR\ninL0dbQzBAicO546qAxPw4kQRq7qd8XkD7r4hoLCA7wCPqYxGaVo5zy8TI7h9O+r\nC5nCvIil6dtgyfMqgS/benKjCTWFqaUK78JB8Q2HZDmUKow0HHS3CovqZjtrFAVD\nCFpVcrOvl+xWtVoFL9xvyxOPQfsfxtCw44nYtO5XvBiW72toYqhjFRHB2lwWlS7g\n3/ZYBevMYkOhsA79kAUWr4SGP/m57iGUVa+9Bz+tR6GbfmMRrY3rNLPp2LR9mR48\nxU3E4fBxs3lXbZjaP7uRC/E26nABMg4nMhiAaU5sCN76o6B1c4IImXhRS+nkjW8f\nXFeNvg/z2PnZwV2dNPHZXNkoX5BUPpIYLA0EE1qQmDDseUlVJckmVTQ/eqqF6VjH\nvRasu40ZERwaf1QDegLW\n=D9w0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-31T02:57:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/e