never blocks on a prompt regardless of env var handling.","tree":{"sha":"24efddb5a4e230783a0bbf44ed0e36e9945bab5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/trees/24efddb5a4e230783a0bbf44ed0e36e9945bab5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/commits/fb44be62c889b187e909cc7fb6fcc8ae3b29c870","verification":{"payload":"tree 24efddb5a4e230783a0bbf44ed0e36e9945bab5c\nparent a7ed93240c99508f3d0c7ca2a19a0a2be53a0941\nauthor aknagar <35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com> 1774880428 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774880428 +0530\n\nfix: add trace logging and exception details to CD test aspire deploy (#65)\n\n* fix: add trace logging and exception details to CD test aspire deploy\n\nAdd --log-level trace and --include-exception-details flags to the\naspire deploy command in the test CD pipeline to diagnose the hang.\n\n* fix: add --non-interactive flag to aspire deploy in CD test pipeline\n\nBelt-and-suspenders alongside DOTNET_ASPIRE_NONINTERACTIVE env var — ensures\nthe CLI itself never blocks on a prompt regardless of env var handling.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpyoasCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlFoQAIbPkfKqTkpkH2e6gOb5IGJ7\ng8WcBUO33JyLyzVlGWzAbI3UPy1+EBbfLoEsXsz7JwgHBZnmSXcTe8UFVsjnFUVp\nu5uQAK6xG9eZb1Po1oRXrj3vhvTsF2Wx7IePg4snD4CDn83LCuJmXIpwr4UapTzq\nPyatCRYXrYSjrbbUJnvIFsXse2tk7b3faWsxRIrOA1NepR2ePVS0ETVF/aj/creF\nmwnZAtj6OWBC8AzWHr1RbEHh/HyDOIsHntudmM1aleUDNSYMi3QTrBf4PnVeN+Ob\nrTFS6JXR7WwNjOSBJWOp91Q/jbCaDFOh5husk557Wg3FKYNt0QGt1RpZu7ppDt0r\nfZMNNpZfGhuvmVUSIjp73VcdEQ8FWf+65NtWVXa/C2+qXSAW97OvlBMntTMhDIUY\nmB2Z9rDFPjtZj9w1zffGWEOKW/7qB4VLPS/GNS53swQIwfVqb84fkyGprLO1y3lK\nedaZSSnEnqtlf/QGDez+v1nnACPFhpQPW5RR+NnfLHH73CvV8Gh+fDhsULrMkZpJ\n/i5ZwCPclJHGTEsCDawlX8Yd5dydeEZm7N+3TnMKCAJ49qZ366Ji5jsKgujJpgGj\nQt2DaUneRekEP3ShHiQ6R/5sdFtxVf7sFUPZOdgVYllF9suT/wnonvW7Zhl7pC4Z\nfjxBhy3xtHSIA3Vququk\n=xT60\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-30T14:20:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/fb44be62c889b187e909cc7fb6fcc8ae3b29c870","node_id":"C_kwDOQv8lUNoAKGZiNDRiZTYyYzg4OWIxODdlOTA5Y2M3ZmI2ZmNjOGFlM2IyOWM4NzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/a7ed93240c99508f3d0c7ca2a19a0a2be53a0941","sha":"a7ed93240c99508f3d0c7ca2a19a0a2be53a0941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/a7ed93240c99508f3d0c7ca2a19a0a2be53a0941"}],"sha":"fb44be62c889b187e909cc7fb6fcc8ae3b29c870","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/fb44be62c889b187e909cc7fb6fcc8ae3b29c870"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35679913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar","id":35679913,"login":"aknagar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc5OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/a7ed93240c99508f3d0c7ca2a19a0a2be53a0941/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-29T18:03:30Z","email":"35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"aknagar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-29T18:03:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/dapr redis host (#63)\n\n* fix: replace ${REDIS_HOST} env-var with localhost in Dapr component YAMLs\n\nWhen running via ''dapr run'' CLI directly (outside .NET Aspire), the REDIS_HOST\nenvironment variable is never set, causing Dapr to connect to '':6379'' (empty host)\ninstead of ''localhost:6379''. This results in a fatal pubsub/statestore init failure.\n\nUsing ''localhost'' as the hardcoded default works for both scenarios:\n- Direct ''dapr run'': connects to local Redis on port 6379\n- Aspire orchestration: .WithMetadata(\"redisHost\", ...) in Program.cs overrides\n  the YAML value at runtime with the actual container host/port, so the YAML\n  default is never used in that flow.\n\n* fix: remove LocalPath from Dapr components so WithMetadata() is applied\n\nWhen LocalPath is set on AddDaprPubSub/AddDaprStateStore, the Aspire lifecycle\nhook passes that YAML file to the Dapr CLI verbatim — it does NOT transform it.\nThis means .WithMetadata() configuration annotations (including the Redis host\nReferenceExpression) are silently ignored, and the static YAML placeholder\n${REDIS_HOST} is passed directly to Dapr, which resolves to an empty string\nand produces the fatal error:\n\n  ''connecting to redis at : dial tcp [::1]:6379: connectex: No connection could\n   be made because the target machine actively refused it''\n\nWithout LocalPath, Aspire generates the component YAML in-memory from scratch,\napplying all WithMetadata() annotations correctly. The Redis host/port from the\nmanaged Redis resource is resolved and injected via a secretKeyRef backed by an\nenv var on the Dapr CLI process.\n\n* fix: add auth.secretStore to pubsub YAML to resolve Dapr Redis host\n\nThe CommunityToolkit.Aspire.Hosting.Dapr package has a bug: when\nWithMetadata(IValueProvider) is used, it correctly generates a\nsecretKeyRef in the component YAML but does NOT add the required\nauth.secretStore field (unlike WithMetadata(ParameterResource) which\ndoes). Without auth.secretStore, Dapr does not know which secret store\nto use to resolve the secretKeyRef, so PUBSUB_REDISHOST resolves to an\nempty string, causing the fatal ''connecting to redis at :'' error.\n\nFix: Add backend/MfePortal.AppHost/.dapr/components/pubsub.yaml as a\nbase template. The Aspire toolkit reads files from {AppHostDir}/.dapr/\ncomponents/ first, applies the WithMetadata() configuration annotations\non top, and preserves the existing auth block from the file. This gives\nus the secretKeyRef (injected by WithMetadata) and auth.secretStore\n(from the base template) in the final generated YAML.\n\nAlso remove the statestore''s WithMetadata(redisHost) since the statestore\ndefaults to state.in-memory for local development and does not use Redis.\n\n* fix(dapr): inject Redis container password into pubsub metadata\n\nAddRedis() (used by RunAsContainer) always generates a random password\nfor the Redis container. Without injecting it, Dapr sends an empty\npassword and Redis closes the TCP connection immediately (EOF error).\n\n- Pass daprRedis.Resource.Password to WithMetadata(\"redisPassword\")\n  so Aspire injects PUBSUB_REDISPASSWORD into the Dapr CLI environment\n- Update pubsub.yaml to reference PUBSUB_REDISPASSWORD via secretKeyRef\n  instead of using a hardcoded empty value: \"\"\n- Only inject password when it''s non-null (Azure Entra ID mode has no password)\n\n* fix: update session end instructions to prevent automatic push and PR creation\n\n* fix: enable TLS for Redis PubSub and update logging level for CommunityToolkit.Aspire\n\n* fix: exclude k6 from publish mode to avoid int arg crash in ProcessValue\n\nk6''s WithScript() passes virtualUsers as a raw System.Int32 to WithArgs().\nThe Azure Container Apps manifest publisher''s ProcessValue() only handles\nstring/EndpointReference/ParameterResource/ReferenceExpression types and\nthrows NotSupportedException on any int value.\n\nThe launchSettings.json profile sets DOTNET_ENVIRONMENT=Development, so\nIsDevelopment() returns true even during --publisher manifest runs. Guard\nthe k6 block with builder.ExecutionContext.IsPublishMode to prevent k6 from\nbeing added to the resource model during manifest generation.\n\n* fix: add Aspire manifest publisher output to .gitignore\n\n* refactor: trim comments in AppHost Program.cs to essentials only","tree":{"sha":"aaee4c8db8e622cb639b3652c9795d6cc19aefc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/trees/aaee4c8db8e622cb639b3652c9795d6cc19aefc8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/commits/a7ed93240c99508f3d0c7ca2a19a0a2be53a0941","verification":{"payload":"tree aaee4c8db8e622cb639b3652c9795d6cc19aefc8\nparent d3bca15beef3a57e65acd0b87a9cbb14398636d8\nauthor aknagar <35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com> 1774807410 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774807410 +0530\n\nFix/dapr redis host (#63)\n\n* fix: replace ${REDIS_HOST} env-var with localhost in Dapr component YAMLs\n\nWhen running via ''dapr run'' CLI directly (outside .NET Aspire), the REDIS_HOST\nenvironment variable is never set, causing Dapr to connect to '':6379'' (empty host)\ninstead of ''localhost:6379''. This results in a fatal pubsub/statestore init failure.\n\nUsing ''localhost'' as the hardcoded default works for both scenarios:\n- Direct ''dapr run'': connects to local Redis on port 6379\n- Aspire orchestration: .WithMetadata(\"redisHost\", ...) in Program.cs overrides\n  the YAML value at runtime with the actual container host/port, so the YAML\n  default is never used in that flow.\n\n* fix: remove LocalPath from Dapr components so WithMetadata() is applied\n\nWhen LocalPath is set on AddDaprPubSub/AddDaprStateStore, the Aspire lifecycle\nhook passes that YAML file to the Dapr CLI verbatim — it does NOT transform it.\nThis means .WithMetadata() configuration annotations (including the Redis host\nReferenceExpression) are silently ignored, and the static YAML placeholder\n${REDIS_HOST} is passed directly to Dapr, which resolves to an empty string\nand produces the fatal error:\n\n  ''connecting to redis at : dial tcp [::1]:6379: connectex: No connection could\n   be made because the target machine actively refused it''\n\nWithout LocalPath, Aspire generates the component YAML in-memory from scratch,\napplying all WithMetadata() annotations correctly. The Redis host/port from the\nmanaged Redis resource is resolved and injected via a secretKeyRef backed by an\nenv var on the Dapr CLI process.\n\n* fix: add auth.secretStore to pubsub YAML to resolve Dapr Redis host\n\nThe CommunityToolkit.Aspire.Hosting.Dapr package has a bug: when\nWithMetadata(IValueProvider) is used, it correctly generates a\nsecretKeyRef in the component YAML but does NOT add the required\nauth.secretStore field (unlike WithMetadata(ParameterResource) which\ndoes). Without auth.secretStore, Dapr does not know which secret store\nto use to resolve the secretKeyRef, so PUBSUB_REDISHOST resolves to an\nempty string, causing the fatal ''connecting to redis at :'' error.\n\nFix: Add backend/MfePortal.AppHost/.dapr/components/pubsub.yaml as a\nbase template. The Aspire toolkit reads files from {AppHostDir}/.dapr/\ncomponents/ first, applies the WithMetadata() configuration annotations\non top, and preserves the existing auth block from the file. This gives\nus the secretKeyRef (injected by WithMetadata) and auth.secretStore\n(from the base template) in the final generated YAML.\n\nAlso remove the statestore''s WithMetadata(redisHost) since the statestore\ndefaults to state.in-memory for local development and does not use Redis.\n\n* fix(dapr): inject Redis container password into pubsub metadata\n\nAddRedis() (used by RunAsContainer) always generates a random password\nfor the Redis container. Without injecting it, Dapr sends an empty\npassword and Redis closes the TCP connection immediately (EOF error).\n\n- Pass daprRedis.Resource.Password to WithMetadata(\"redisPassword\")\n  so Aspire injects PUBSUB_REDISPASSWORD into the Dapr CLI environment\n- Update pubsub.yaml to reference PUBSUB_REDISPASSWORD via secretKeyRef\n  instead of using a hardcoded empty value: \"\"\n- Only inject password when it''s non-null (Azure Entra ID mode has no password)\n\n* fix: update session end instructions to prevent automatic push and PR creation\n\n* fix: enable TLS for Redis PubSub and update logging level for CommunityToolkit.Aspire\n\n* fix: exclude k6 from publish mode to avoid int arg crash in ProcessValue\n\nk6''s WithScript() passes virtualUsers as a raw System.Int32 to WithArgs().\nThe Azure Container Apps manifest publisher''s ProcessValue() only handles\nstring/EndpointReference/ParameterResource/ReferenceExpression types and\nthrows NotSupportedException on any int value.\n\nThe launchSettings.json profile sets DOTNET_ENVIRONMENT=Development, so\nIsDevelopment() returns true even during --publisher manifest runs. Guard\nthe k6 block with builder.ExecutionContext.IsPublishMode to prevent k6 from\nbeing added to the resource model during manifest generation.\n\n* fix: add Aspire manifest publisher output to .gitignore\n\n* refactor: trim comments in AppHost Program.cs to essentials only","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpyWlyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlgwQAFUKbnF5GpadEl4DE7HDe8dv\nnPAA4w42t1C6NYu4AyBRG/czSkDNYuZHTaEuH/pRf2DWg0nBpgzgvNzBuYMQGOU2\nK++2eCJo+dAAc+taKb1cNCHCtOCrlt0BWq9JBd87C3DEHJczyeXT+nNU0dD9mcZz\nVdl3QacowUrr1VQYorUURHEXDuDFe00T3lswbOy/Xmdy0mbXYHQ7FtOAgfU1Azo8\nYK0avWAWxhy+Ao3FzCKrQueOaFvIHacavswnyaxsxl7fuD3JAiWbpqurqinjdCNi\nBbx3x7+AhzP7KugUjN55QCeaA8IlUHAB0uA0CwTZ/ChfgW3ysnlxYgnGF4nUMQC7\nfgymBpTvFT6LUV7Ps0ia1OiQjCuo1uhUEmq4M5FMHUgafteA1bQ5qXkTqXpGHlSZ\n+Rs9rllYEJQjemIKhKi/O/W9xmA3biTyEYNgBmleTb1I1fFUndd1NtNTxWfGJYaZ\nclczLk0Uqhg1GZ58wqjIKq+YmX4pt77z2gB3o6pZhKW9kFBAXt+vS/+5d2S8sO3/\n8EhI3yp95OEDh1tsF4kJ+vl7GB+tww9nA6vEjWmPa3c69qeoHJNeZvx8fU62BFxa\ndD+ne7xRvS4uIlZw0cmsRXK3XCFUgl2UN+u2QbVUv01piI3esLlHtopph9HsyvbD\nEq68+AG1RF/QMSxRmuh7\n=adeE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-29T18:03:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/a7ed93240c99508f3d0c7ca2a19a0a2be53a0941","node