","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/6e4cf475d713ea7c94dc2ba8cc3838693ac0d7fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-22T16:38:10Z","email":"35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"aknagar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-22T16:38:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(devcontainer): install postgresql-client, extend PATH to zsh, remove stale image pulls (#58)\n\n- Add postgresql-client to Dockerfile: post-start.sh uses psql to wait for\n  PostgreSQL readiness but the package was never installed, causing the health\n  check to fail silently (command not found) or error at startup.\n\n- Extend .dapr/bin and .dotnet/tools PATH entries to ~/.zshrc as well as\n  ~/.bashrc: devcontainer.json sets zsh as the default shell, so without this\n  the aspire and dapr CLIs are not on PATH in interactive zsh terminals.\n\n- Remove mssql/server:2022-latest pre-pull: the project uses PostgreSQL exclusively;\n  SQL Server was never referenced in Program.cs or any .cs file. Pulling it only\n  wastes ~1.7 GB of bandwidth on every new devcontainer build.\n\n- Remove servicebus-emulator:latest pre-pull: Aspire.Hosting.Azure.ServiceBus\n  manages its own pinned image version (currently 1.1.2). Pulling :latest\n  alongside a version-pinned pull adds unnecessary bandwidth and can silently\n  diverge from the version Aspire actually uses.","tree":{"sha":"dc5569cd61b885326b737a12b86f2b5b03bfc4a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/trees/dc5569cd61b885326b737a12b86f2b5b03bfc4a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/commits/6e4cf475d713ea7c94dc2ba8cc3838693ac0d7fe","verification":{"payload":"tree dc5569cd61b885326b737a12b86f2b5b03bfc4a5\nparent a9450598d845706310779ccbbb16427d8b1c203f\nauthor aknagar <35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com> 1774197490 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774197490 +0530\n\nfix(devcontainer): install postgresql-client, extend PATH to zsh, remove stale image pulls (#58)\n\n- Add postgresql-client to Dockerfile: post-start.sh uses psql to wait for\n  PostgreSQL readiness but the package was never installed, causing the health\n  check to fail silently (command not found) or error at startup.\n\n- Extend .dapr/bin and .dotnet/tools PATH entries to ~/.zshrc as well as\n  ~/.bashrc: devcontainer.json sets zsh as the default shell, so without this\n  the aspire and dapr CLIs are not on PATH in interactive zsh terminals.\n\n- Remove mssql/server:2022-latest pre-pull: the project uses PostgreSQL exclusively;\n  SQL Server was never referenced in Program.cs or any .cs file. Pulling it only\n  wastes ~1.7 GB of bandwidth on every new devcontainer build.\n\n- Remove servicebus-emulator:latest pre-pull: Aspire.Hosting.Azure.ServiceBus\n  manages its own pinned image version (currently 1.1.2). Pulling :latest\n  alongside a version-pinned pull adds unnecessary bandwidth and can silently\n  diverge from the version Aspire actually uses.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwBryCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdMgQAGIwAQb8HyNUogt90pamasBH\nCA18emchbOqzRaJtDdrZHXln31MyaJ87xVEroM4Bxz6Ppm3gxyVKwKyix5Yu0FFl\n+aHc2xSKxqR3FcmHADy9S2T5iF8xien1Q27EhPtMo76zSYh5s98XEPD7f57Aam/z\nq88oIYtlwHCAxdLzlKdhzyB64iAH51LlwR7gWboHinHGrEQT9hs5NS688RdoiNwD\norCGibwkYpI8rY37LImmHSC4nKHLXgejA7sgb2Lcgvcei2bzFzCia5ossibqWVg9\n1EiUb3uoZEztNUaMbwBHHp6n2GCc6ZUgK48KhCnsHIShluJTb6J7DvnF4bjnAuCi\nWQRYQ4AVaB1KWTbqe7rTvNuRsw4SALsd0v4FFcQPw2VD6Z9Ht7Hdpo3KPQ4Hv0gW\n/5rTRbk2sM1YwqGHZDISH52J8gU7GhbbAp1o6Bf3zDJlGpNBxtMM+Ur/Vj+GFHJg\nli/U5725u4LeijqZPbEjQOu6INV2VEQBMm9yOZzbIoimt6dGJQ3IWWiCWNShCKaT\nmP4NvODRoMCGKdsYGUjXYtYIoY5eV1IxAHeHjGclnkpn/wZHBDB9tlML7gq86nL1\nCv29qLdcGfBukI43iAPSyEK//9zljmrvYcpog2hSBbT3vpH3YPbE0nAeR54+hqpd\nAhnolWs/EMITuE2YzBV6\n=X1CL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-22T16:38:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/6e4cf475d713ea7c94dc2ba8cc3838693ac0d7fe","node_id":"C_kwDOQv8lUNoAKDZlNGNmNDc1ZDcxM2VhN2M5NGRjMmJhOGNjMzgzODY5M2FjMGQ3ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/a9450598d845706310779ccbbb16427d8b1c203f","sha":"a9450598d845706310779ccbbb16427d8b1c203f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/a9450598d845706310779ccbbb16427d8b1c203f"}],"sha":"6e4cf475d713ea7c94dc2ba8cc3838693ac0d7fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/6e4cf475d713ea7c94dc2ba8cc3838693ac0d7fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35679913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar","id":35679913,"login":"aknagar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc5OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/a9450598d845706310779ccbbb16427d8b1c203f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-22T16:05:33Z","email":"35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"aknagar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-22T16:05:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/devcontainer ssl cert (#57)\n\n* fix: configure SSL_CERT_DIR so OpenSSL trusts ASP.NET Core dev-cert in devcontainer\n\nOn Linux, dotnet dev-certs places the PEM cert in $HOME/.aspnet/dev-certs/trust/\nbut OpenSSL does not include that directory in its default cert search path.\nThis caused the warning about SSL_CERT_DIR needing to be updated.\n\n- post-create.sh: after trusting the cert, write SSL_CERT_DIR to ~/.bashrc,\n  ~/.zshrc, and /etc/environment so all interactive and non-interactive\n  processes pick it up across container restarts.\n- devcontainer.json: add SSL_CERT_DIR to remoteEnv so VS Code and its\n  child processes (language servers, terminals) inherit it immediately\n  without waiting for a shell profile to be sourced.\n\n* fix: use sudo for /etc/docker operations in post-create.sh\n\nThe script runs as the non-root ''vscode'' user, so bare mkdir/write to\n/etc/docker failed with ''Permission denied''. All three operations that\ntouch /etc/docker (mkdir, mv, write) now use sudo, consistent with the\nexisting sudo usage for /etc/environment.\n\n* fix: redirect MSBuild obj/bin to /tmp in devcontainer to fix timestamp permission errors\n\nWhen the workspace is bind-mounted from a Windows host, MSBuild cannot set\nfile timestamps on the NTFS-backed paths (e.g. *.Up2Date sentinel files),\nproducing ''Access to the path … is denied'' (MSB3374).\n\nDirectory.Build.props is picked up automatically by every project under\nbackend/. When DOTNET_RUNNING_IN_CONTAINER=true it redirects\nBaseIntermediateOutputPath and BaseOutputPath to /tmp/msbuild/<project>/,\nwhich is a container-native tmpfs/overlay filesystem with no NTFS\nrestrictions. On developer machines and in CI the variable is unset so\nstandard next-to-project obj/ and bin/ paths are used unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"7e87c80e85529abd9db88aee3d9af6f618a00933","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/trees/7e87c80e85529abd9db88aee3d9af6f618a00933"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/commits/a9450598d845706310779ccbbb16427d8b1c203f","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e87c80e85529abd9db88aee3d9af6f618a00933\nparent dedd27daf8fb96a4639c9097952392513f493c19\nauthor aknagar <35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com> 1774195533 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774195533 +0530\n\nFix/devcontainer ssl cert (#57)\n\n* fix: configure SSL_CERT_DIR so OpenSSL trusts ASP.NET Core dev-cert in devcontainer\n\nOn Linux, dotnet dev-certs places the PEM cert in $HOME/.aspnet/dev-certs/trust/\nbut OpenSSL does not include that directory in its default cert search path.\nThis caused the warning about SSL_CERT_DIR needing to be updated.\n\n- post-create.sh: after trusting the cert, write SSL_CERT_DIR to ~/.bashrc,\n  ~/.zshrc, and /etc/environment so all interactive and non-interactive\n  processes pick it up across container restarts.\n- devcontainer.json: add SSL_CERT_DIR to remoteEnv so VS Code and its\n  child processes (language servers, terminals) inherit it immediately\n  without waiting for a shell profile to be sourced.\n\n* fix: use sudo for /etc/docker operations in post-create.sh\n\nThe script runs as the non-root ''vscode'' user, so bare mkdir/write to\n/etc/docker failed with ''Permission denied''. All three operations that\ntouch /etc/docker (mkdir, mv, write) now use sudo, consistent with the\nexisting sudo usage for /etc/environment.\n\n* fix: redirect MSBuild obj/bin to /tmp in devcontainer to fix timestamp permission errors\n\nWhen the workspace is bind-mounted from a Windows host, MSBuild cannot set\nfile timestamps on the NTFS-backed paths (e.g. *.Up2Date sentinel files),\nproducing ''Access to the path … is denied'' (MSB3374).\n\nDirectory.Build.props is picked up automatically by every project under\nbackend/. When DOTNET_RUNNING_IN_CONTAINER=true it redirects\nBaseIntermediateOutputPath and BaseOutputPath to /tmp/msbuild/<project>/,\nwhich is a container-native tmpfs/overlay filesystem with no NTFS\nrestrictions. On developer machines and in CI the variable is unset so\nstandard next-to-project obj/ and bin/ paths are used unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwBNNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvTcQAA4Y21E+7BOxZZqBjkE9CJJZ\nRK8tvmrDYzm80duBQx5vP4t8SGqCD1c95oUc37/OG33rAysAwSEX9ZyN9OIdI4YK\n1NsQrTnH1FYCrOxEVNDF9tDAKvamxALG6Vxa1CaUCvux0eH9+6NS+WSFq6ahju7e\n7EVOckjl7eDxIPlDip0VRLeuVijj2zmcj8vciKYnUf2PacnEQZw0YIHDdUiksWXN\nk54WPnYc/tHGxo+5323a2ZAdsGbNk6JjpF5DBJOwx12av3GH/IjfHHe3rPUEURAM\nxDzThVee7Mj1dkXyZSzcX3ARnSal0YdHUqQBbspgcozzV1qH5l/ahjD8WIlEX5tz\nffmE6gyTEZihyLHqPPVXR6MrsXF6Cv1GHR7iESypeCTm3E44UDqyGVlgaD1OULJc\npVmy8WA/ewveu1RZVji9qyI6hkjlW0OzGK7LDmWdJ8e/Gz6egaG1wkAv9h7yLAJl\nOlcvb1Gt43nn1WjsR9uxHeyd83WX1lBTHlxppcGdpVV7eY6yKKgqjz/mOegKSNVV\nGpPrrQuYuSwsZWm1aYBPXtDqtFN6/koSufqwRYkkJkVms4eYafpI28DVAji26iIo\nRvAfkZ5ReWsKAdFlbdXTxmZhHc53jA2UkPNhyawD8uqzTnm1H4P