tarred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/8ccf30a630d55d1f7cdbc388b8c34bffa6345d52","node_id":"C_kwDOQv8lUNoAKDhjY2YzMGE2MzBkNTVkMWY3Y2RiYzM4OGI4YzM0YmZmYTYzNDVkNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/444754a6125fda6545e47a7a010a395f0272067f","sha":"444754a6125fda6545e47a7a010a395f0272067f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/444754a6125fda6545e47a7a010a395f0272067f"}],"sha":"8ccf30a630d55d1f7cdbc388b8c34bffa6345d52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/8ccf30a630d55d1f7cdbc388b8c34bffa6345d52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35679913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar","id":35679913,"login":"aknagar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc5OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/444754a6125fda6545e47a7a010a395f0272067f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-22T08:41:44Z","email":"35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"aknagar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-22T08:41:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/devcontainer aspire health (#47)\n\n* feat(opencode): add /run-ci-backend slash command\n\nAdds a local CI pipeline slash command that builds the backend solution,\nruns unit tests with code coverage (excluding Integration/E2E/LoadTest),\ngenerates a ReportGenerator report, and displays a formatted tabular\nsummary of build status, test results, and per-assembly coverage.\n\n* docs: document git worktree workflow in docs/GIT.md\n\n* docs: trim GIT.md to branching strategy only\n\n* docs: replace branching strategy with worktree branching workflow\n\n* chore: lower coverage threshold from 80% to 75%\n\n* feat(devcontainer): increase Aspire dashboard wait timeout to 120s, add token extractor\n\n* feat(devcontainer): add Aspire resource health polling and table display functions\n\n* fix(devcontainer): declare response variable before while loop in wait_for_aspire_resources\n\n* fix(devcontainer): fix resource count accuracy, use python3 for table parsing, improve function safety\n\n* feat(devcontainer): wire Aspire resource health polling and portal URL into startup flow\n\n* fix(devcontainer): use C-style for loop to avoid seq subshell and variable leakage\n\n* feat(devcontainer): forward Aspire Resource Service port 18889, fix port 22028 label\n\n* fix(devcontainer): handle empty resource list, fix table alignment, improve total count accuracy\n\n* Fix: replace ''&& break/continue'' with if/then to avoid set -e silent kill\n\nUnder ''set -e'', ''[ condition ] && break'' returns exit 1 when the condition\nis false, causing the script to exit silently before reaching the dashboard\nURL banner. Replace both occurrences with ''if [ condition ]; then ...; fi''\nwhich never produces a non-zero exit from the conditional logic itself.\n\n* Fix: move token extraction after resource wait, extend retry to 60s\n\nThe ''Login to the dashboard at ...?t=TOKEN'' line is emitted when the\ndashboard ResourceReadyEvent fires, which can be seconds to minutes into\nstartup. The previous 10s window ran before resources were ready, so the\ntoken was never in the log yet.\n\nMove extraction to after wait_for_aspire_resources (which waits up to 300s)\nand extend the retry to 60s. Also pass empty token to the resource poller\nsince the API endpoint does not require auth on localhost.\n\n* Switch to ''aspire run --detach --format json'' for AppHost startup\n\n- post-create.sh: install Aspire.Cli global tool and add ~/.dotnet/tools to PATH\n- post-start.sh: replace ''nohup dotnet run'' + log-file token scraping with\n  ''aspire run --detach --non-interactive --format json'', which exits immediately\n  and returns a JSON payload containing dashboardUrl (with ?t=TOKEN) and\n  appHostPid directly — no log parsing needed\n- Remove get_aspire_token() and the 60s token retry loop entirely\n- Simplify wait_for_aspire_resources() signature (token param removed;\n  dashboard API does not require auth on localhost)","tree":{"sha":"155a1d677d6343c3be00713f9eac76aa6069611e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/trees/155a1d677d6343c3be00713f9eac76aa6069611e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/commits/444754a6125fda6545e47a7a010a395f0272067f","verification":{"payload":"tree 155a1d677d6343c3be00713f9eac76aa6069611e\nparent 415a536b3c5d7f638083446df7347d458af70059\nauthor aknagar <35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com> 1774168904 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774168904 +0530\n\nFeat/devcontainer aspire health (#47)\n\n* feat(opencode): add /run-ci-backend slash command\n\nAdds a local CI pipeline slash command that builds the backend solution,\nruns unit tests with code coverage (excluding Integration/E2E/LoadTest),\ngenerates a ReportGenerator report, and displays a formatted tabular\nsummary of build status, test results, and per-assembly coverage.\n\n* docs: document git worktree workflow in docs/GIT.md\n\n* docs: trim GIT.md to branching strategy only\n\n* docs: replace branching strategy with worktree branching workflow\n\n* chore: lower coverage threshold from 80% to 75%\n\n* feat(devcontainer): increase Aspire dashboard wait timeout to 120s, add token extractor\n\n* feat(devcontainer): add Aspire resource health polling and table display functions\n\n* fix(devcontainer): declare response variable before while loop in wait_for_aspire_resources\n\n* fix(devcontainer): fix resource count accuracy, use python3 for table parsing, improve function safety\n\n* feat(devcontainer): wire Aspire resource health polling and portal URL into startup flow\n\n* fix(devcontainer): use C-style for loop to avoid seq subshell and variable leakage\n\n* feat(devcontainer): forward Aspire Resource Service port 18889, fix port 22028 label\n\n* fix(devcontainer): handle empty resource list, fix table alignment, improve total count accuracy\n\n* Fix: replace ''&& break/continue'' with if/then to avoid set -e silent kill\n\nUnder ''set -e'', ''[ condition ] && break'' returns exit 1 when the condition\nis false, causing the script to exit silently before reaching the dashboard\nURL banner. Replace both occurrences with ''if [ condition ]; then ...; fi''\nwhich never produces a non-zero exit from the conditional logic itself.\n\n* Fix: move token extraction after resource wait, extend retry to 60s\n\nThe ''Login to the dashboard at ...?t=TOKEN'' line is emitted when the\ndashboard ResourceReadyEvent fires, which can be seconds to minutes into\nstartup. The previous 10s window ran before resources were ready, so the\ntoken was never in the log yet.\n\nMove extraction to after wait_for_aspire_resources (which waits up to 300s)\nand extend the retry to 60s. Also pass empty token to the resource poller\nsince the API endpoint does not require auth on localhost.\n\n* Switch to ''aspire run --detach --format json'' for AppHost startup\n\n- post-create.sh: install Aspire.Cli global tool and add ~/.dotnet/tools to PATH\n- post-start.sh: replace ''nohup dotnet run'' + log-file token scraping with\n  ''aspire run --detach --non-interactive --format json'', which exits immediately\n  and returns a JSON payload containing dashboardUrl (with ?t=TOKEN) and\n  appHostPid directly — no log parsing needed\n- Remove get_aspire_token() and the 60s token retry loop entirely\n- Simplify wait_for_aspire_resources() signature (token param removed;\n  dashboard API does not require auth on localhost)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpv6tICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGxAQAEIaBGdIAatftUC6UMPXslx3\nuMmZyWQ907rZ70zLYmH6HFrqJV6c7blp/Pf4xcRpnvNkK/VURxo3/qRSEpjcfvYT\ncj07n0ZlEqvVNqQZb3yyfKtAtX3FIcLX38T/aVoPiWogLst2LCuOjwF7JKOvx5fi\nw4xPg4Ow7IGvVKQOtq23I1wp0VOohstuAtXv8OXa6E0MwQvqT+8wamt0hQBF+blG\no0Dl63tfwGFCpsdoEN9RwRZqqkQjhrIJ3JjCwBGoBjQdcWFS+Xtw7HM1SjJ42ADT\nC8DKHV4m5lPzla1Kw45oxMt6icooX7jaPiLu69k3/dDDBsqeEMHk+EMrTdaIEZV7\niBQfD+L68J7WS8z9OY7f5HQYfX5KaJOo5jw82AjgM413Jk96LZLoQSISOoTwrTv2\nveUjhXIpQu0vPQi9Km70jtwI4cRpUhYzmq5RhLzmJjfBMLx1gD5tmEtNqXR91zUb\n4xYlQDfblUIlyee4al3nXkZX0dXtolJG/RkfIzsLrZz1VjJuC5lR2y/DlgMCQMQk\nmZ2yXQhop8Xdw32t8nq61C5GS/C3uhunEU3glknmzM8U2Tdpvecwj0YAkaOEjWnw\nrv6HRl4QaJobrjvD4B1XLM3voap1bnRO/v6k3XBsvYy5kf+4HOZE8e/EyULMQqub\nZdp7uvcl0YX/hFMmxkHs\n=pM2e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-22T08:41:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-f