3","node_id":"C_kwDOQv8lUNoAKDViYjM2MGFlN2YzNzdlMDQ2YzE1ODI4ZTJmZjMxY2EyZDhhZjA3YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar/mfe-portal/commit/9e58914398c7617762d948261d1128803d7caafb","sha":"9e58914398c7617762d948261d1128803d7caafb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/9e58914398c7617762d948261d1128803d7caafb"}],"sha":"5bb360ae7f377e046c15828e2ff31ca2d8af07a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/5bb360ae7f377e046c15828e2ff31ca2d8af07a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35679913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aknagar","id":35679913,"login":"aknagar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Njc5OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aknagar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/commits/9e58914398c7617762d948261d1128803d7caafb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-21T18:57:56Z","email":"35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"aknagar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-21T18:57:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: add timeouts and missing Aspire workload step to infra provision… (#29)\n\n* fix: add timeouts and missing Aspire workload step to infra provision pipelines\n\n- Add job-level timeout-minutes: 45 to both infra provision workflows to prevent\n  silent hangs from consuming the 6-hour GitHub Actions default\n- Add step-level timeouts: 10min for workload install, 5min for CLI install,\n  30min for aspire deploy\n- Add missing ''dotnet workload install aspire'' step to test workflow (was only\n  present in prod, causing aspire deploy to hang downloading workload on-demand)\n- Fix prod workflow using wrong AZURE_CLIENT_ID (test identity) — changed to\n  AZURE_CLIENT_ID_PROD to use the correct production service principal\n\n* fix: upgrade azure/login to v2 and pin diagrid-dashboard image tag\n\n- Upgrade azure/login from v1 to v2 across all 7 workflows (9 occurrences total):\n  cd-backend-deploy-prod, cd-backend-deploy-test, cd-deploy-prod,\n  cd-frontend-deploy-prod (x2), cd-frontend-deploy-test (x2),\n  infra-provision-prod, infra-provision-test\n  v2 runs on Node 20 with security improvements over the deprecated v1\n- Pin diagrid-dashboard container image from :latest to :0.0.1\n  to prevent unexpected breaking changes from uncontrolled upstream updates\n\n* fix: harden OIDC setup, redact hardcoded Azure IDs, add prod env gate\n\nsetup-github-oidc.ps1:\n- Replace Owner role with Contributor + conditionally-scoped User Access\n  Administrator so the pipeline can create managed identity role assignments\n  (AcrPull, Service Bus Data Owner, Key Vault Secrets User) without having\n  unrestricted Owner rights over the whole subscription\n- Remove wildcard federated credential (repo:*) that allowed any branch or\n  PR to obtain an Azure token; replace with explicit credentials for:\n  * main branch (ref:refs/heads/main)\n  * production GitHub environment (environment:production)\n  * test GitHub environment (environment:test)\n\nfrontend.parameters.json:\n- Replace real Azure subscription ID (bc721a0b-...), resource group name,\n  Container Apps environment ID, ACR endpoint, and managed identity resource\n  ID with __PLACEHOLDER__ tokens so no live infrastructure identifiers are\n  stored in source control\n\ninfra-provision-prod.yml:\n- Add ''environment: production'' to the provision job so GitHub requires\n  reviewer approval and enforces environment protection rules before any\n  destructive infrastructure changes are applied to production\n\n* fix: add timeout-minutes to health-check jobs in prod deploy pipelines\n\nPrevents DNS-hang or slow-curl scenarios from blocking GitHub-hosted\nrunners indefinitely. Both cd-deploy-prod.yml and\ncd-backend-deploy-prod.yml health-check jobs now have a hard\ntimeout-minutes: 15 ceiling (worst-case manual retry loop is ~360 s,\nwell inside the 15-min window).\n\n* fix: harden Bicep IaC — parameterise ACR SKU, cap replicas, secure AppInsights, fix Log Analytics divergence\n\n- infra-acr.bicep: replace hardcoded Basic SKU with skuName param\n  (default ''Basic'') so prod can pass ''Standard'' at deploy time\n- augmentservice.bicep: add maxReplicas:10 to scale block; move\n  APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING from plain env value to a\n  named secret + secretRef (consistent with redis-uri pattern)\n- infra.module.bicep: remove inline Log Analytics workspace creation;\n  accept logs_infra_outputs_name param and reference existing workspace\n  via ''existing'' keyword — eliminates split-telemetry risk\n- postgres.bicep, redis.bicep: add maxReplicas:1 (stateless containers\n  must not scale); add warning comment about missing persistent storage","tree":{"sha":"37ac2ca64e7fc4bca2fdce7d4801bae2209d3262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/trees/37ac2ca64e7fc4bca2fdce7d4801bae2209d3262"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aknagar/mfe-portal/git/commits/9e58914398c7617762d948261d1128803d7caafb","verification":{"payload":"tree 37ac2ca64e7fc4bca2fdce7d4801bae2209d3262\nparent ee2e410a0b8c60af1eea54919ac52d7f6e3e8338\nauthor aknagar <35679913+aknagar@users.noreply.github.com> 1774119476 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774119476 +0530\n\nfix: add timeouts and missing Aspire workload step to infra provision… (#29)\n\n* fix: add timeouts and missing Aspire workload step to infra provision pipelines\n\n- Add job-level timeout-minutes: 45 to both infra provision workflows to prevent\n  silent hangs from consuming the 6-hour GitHub Actions default\n- Add step-level timeouts: 10min for workload install, 5min for CLI install,\n  30min for aspire deploy\n- Add missing ''dotnet workload install aspire'' step to test workflow (was only\n  present in prod, causing aspire deploy to hang downloading workload on-demand)\n- Fix prod workflow using wrong AZURE_CLIENT_ID (test identity) — changed to\n  AZURE_CLIENT_ID_PROD to use the correct production service principal\n\n* fix: upgrade azure/login to v2 and pin diagrid-dashboard image tag\n\n- Upgrade azure/login from v1 to v2 across all 7 workflows (9 occurrences total):\n  cd-backend-deploy-prod, cd-backend-deploy-test, cd-deploy-prod,\n  cd-frontend-deploy-prod (x2), cd-frontend-deploy-test (x2),\n  infra-provision-prod, infra-provision-test\n  v2 runs on Node 20 with security improvements over the deprecated v1\n- Pin diagrid-dashboard container image from :latest to :0.0.1\n  to prevent unexpected breaking changes from uncontrolled upstream updates\n\n* fix: harden OIDC setup, redact hardcoded Azure IDs, add prod env gate\n\nsetup-github-oidc.ps1:\n- Replace Owner role with Contributor + conditionally-scoped User Access\n  Administrator so the pipeline can create managed identity role assignments\n  (AcrPull, Service Bus Data Owner, Key Vault Secrets User) without having\n  unrestricted Owner rights over the whole subscription\n- Remove wildcard federated credential (repo:*) that allowed any branch or\n  PR to obtain an Azure token; replace with explicit credentials for:\n  * main branch (ref:refs/heads/main)\n  * production GitHub environment (environment:production)\n  * test GitHub environment (environment:test)\n\nfrontend.parameters.json:\n- Replace real Azure subscription ID (bc721a0b-...), resource group name,\n  Container Apps environment ID, ACR endpoint, and managed identity resource\n  ID with __PLACEHOLDER__ tokens so no live infrastructure identifiers are\n  stored in source control\n\ninfra-provision-prod.yml:\n- Add ''environment: production'' to the provision job so GitHub requires\n  reviewer approval and enforces environment protection rules before any\n  destructive infrastructure changes are applied to production\n\n* fix: add timeout-minutes to health-check jobs in prod deploy pipelines\n\nPrevents DNS-hang or slow-curl scenarios from blocking GitHub-hosted\nrunners indefinitely. Both cd-deploy-prod.yml and\ncd-backend-deploy-prod.yml health-check jobs now have a hard\ntimeout-minutes: 15 ceiling (worst-case manual retry loop is ~360 s,\nwell inside the 15-min window).\n\n* fix: harden Bicep IaC — parameterise ACR SKU, cap replicas, secure AppInsights, fix Log Analytics divergence\n\n- infra-acr.bicep: replace hardcoded Basic SKU with skuName param\n  (default ''Basic'') so prod can pass ''Standard'' at deploy time\n- augmentservice.bicep: add maxReplicas:10 to scale block; move\n  APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING from plain env value to a\n  named secret + secretRef (consistent with redis-uri pattern)\n- infra.module.bicep: remove inline Log Analytics workspace creation;\n  accept logs_infra_outputs_name param and reference existing workspace\n  via ''existing'' keyword — eliminates split-telemetry risk\n- postgres.bicep, redis.bicep: add maxReplicas:1 (stateless containers\n  must not scale); add warning comment about missing persistent storage","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpvuo1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA14sQAC67x0UXnn+V4NiDvOYwqE/a\nU4A1zzzMydXWNh+uJRMQUZl0fdt+7cmQKlE4lJTo1+TiODfDc3P/FjceBhHHp3Y2\nJK8Oc8Mgr+2ko4a8meEm2rADqAquhor4glVWNsRMDA+BM7qL/RCwNV3mr62HHlxo\nTAdGvl0UCCcr1QzzmJf2CInTkzCtY6x5ekk9OP+Rhx8NPSXFvq6ow2iBiUHXetYi\n4PheryHQXDOeVltCSKPoleVluvPQfGF5D44Wu1IVdsX78Fd